{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[operator-attested] EVIDENCE for the gate criteria.\n\nGERRIT: change 1670 (\"Deprecate the orphaned resolved_statuses keys\"),\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1670 — 19 files changed, +218/-102.\n\nLOCAL COMMANDS, run in worktree /Users/joeoakhart/macaw-prawn with the worktree venv on PATH\n(env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"), at commit 77cdff2cdd:\n\n  $ make lint\n  All checks passed!  /  1926 files already formatted\n  python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check\n  active=61 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n  zizmor: No findings to report.  /  actionlint (all workflows)\n\n  $ make typecheck\n  mypy src/rebar scripts\n  Success: no issues found in 509 source files\n\n  $ python scripts/check_config_reads.py\n  Config-read gate: OK (_config_schema.py — all dataclass fields are read).\n  (with the two expected advisory notices that both `# read-via:` markers point at the still-\n  open follow-up f408-64ad-ee41-46b6)\n\n  $ python -m pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py \\\n      tests/unit/test_config_resolved_statuses_deprecation.py \\\n      tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py \\\n      tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py -q\n  56 passed in 18.47s\n\n  $ python -m pytest tests/unit tests/scripts -q     # full sweep\n  6283 passed, 11 skipped\n\nNOTE ON THE MODULE-SIZE GATE, recorded because it changed the design. The full sweep initially\nFAILED test_no_src_module_over_the_hard_cap: _config_schema.py was already at 798 LOC against\nthe 800 hard cap, and the new warning helper pushed it to 824. Rather than baseline or shave\ncomments, the helper moved to `_deprecations.py` as `warn_deprecated_cfg_keys` — the correct\ncall-graph seam, since it is registry logic and `_config_schema` already imports from\n`_deprecations` (no cycle). `_config_schema.py` is back to 798 LOC, i.e. this change is\nsize-neutral on that file, and `_deprecations.py` sits at 419.\n\nTwo other findings folded in during implementation:\n* The plan-review's advisory A1 finding was ADOPTED — no parallel table of deprecated keys;\n  the registry is consulted directly.\n* Extracting the helper also resolved a C901 regression (coerce_sparse 15 -> 16), so the\n  complexity baseline shows new=0 rather than absorbing new debt.\n\nClosing waits on Verified +1 on 1670, per the project's CI-before-close rule."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786562508923266001,"uuid":"7d822da4-90f3-432f-9b4c-0fbf98776c0f"}